{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792263820,"nonce":"X3yyXH5TWY+baK9p9nsKbC3FXo8=","title":"CodeEditor's gutter and content stop at the code's height when it is shorter than the view","message":"**What**\n\nIn components/haxe/ashui/components/CodeEditor.hx the content (.ui-code-content) and the gutter (.ui-code-gutter) take height={contentHeight}, which is the lines times the line height plus padding. When the code is shorter than the view, the gutter's border and background end where the code does while the frame runs on below. Seen in ChimpMonk's Behaviours Haxe tab: 15 lines in a tall view.\n\n**Workaround**\n\nChimpMonk adds `.ui-code-content, .ui-code-gutter { min-height: 100% }` in its own stylesheet.\n\n**Fix**\n\nMake the gutter, and the content, at least the viewport's height in CodeEditor itself, so the workaround can go. The scroll extent must stay the code's own height when it is longer than the view.\n\nReported by the ChimpMonk session (chimpmonk-af) on 2026-10-17.","files":null}]}